# Red-proofs (09-send-identity S1, Refs #9)

For EACH of the four REQ-S2 forgery tests, the forgery was temporarily
re-introduced (sabotage), the corresponding test turned RED, then the tree
was reverted. Clean-tree reruns are green (see S1 acceptance below).

## S1a — spoofed --source ignored
- Sabotage: `scripts/send_identity.py` attested return changed to
  `sender=claimed_source or sender` (records the client claim).
- Test: `AttestationVerifyTests.test_spoofed_claimed_source_is_ignored`
- Result: RED (`AssertionError: 'red-actor@other-rig' != 'blue-probe@test-rig'`
  — the forged claim was recorded). Reverted via backup copy; rerun OK.

## S1b — replay rejected
- Sabotage: replay gate disabled
  (`if nonce in seen and False:` in `verify_attestation`).
- Test: `AttestationVerifyTests.test_replay_of_valid_attestation_is_rejected`
- Result: RED (second presentation accepted as `attested` instead of
  `rejected`). Reverted via backup copy; rerun OK.

## S1c — cross-rig impersonation impossible
- Sabotage: scope gate disabled
  (`if rig != expected_rig and False:` in `verify_attestation`).
- Test: `AttestationVerifyTests.test_cross_rig_presentation_fails_scope`
- Result: RED (rig-Y presentation of a rig-X attestation verified).
  Reverted via backup copy; rerun OK.

## S1d — bare-send bypass still denied
- Sabotage: first `      - rig send` deny line removed from
  `fleet/fleet.yaml` (working tree only, no regen — the corpus test reads
  the fleet file directly).
- Test: `BareSendDenyTests.test_fleet_declares_exact_bare_deny_triple`
- Result: RED (`roles missing exact bash_deny triple: ['a11y-specialist']`).
  Reverted via `git checkout -- fleet/fleet.yaml`; rerun OK.

